<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Scope" id="Scope">

    <web-summary>
        Choose which workspace %tool_name% works on with --scope: nearest, topmost or global. Find and jump to any
        project with %tool_call% search and the gcd shortcut.
    </web-summary>

    <p>
        The scope tells %tool_name% which workspace to use as the root of a command. Set it with
        <code>-s</code> or <code>--scope</code>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="Values" id="scope_chapter-values">
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td>Scope</td>
                <td>Root workspace</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>nearest</code> (default)</td>
                <td>The first workspace found going up from the current folder.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>topmost</code></td>
                <td>The highest workspace found going up from the current folder.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>global</code></td>
                <td>The global workspace of <path>~/.gws</path>, wherever you are.</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
        <p>
            A command works on the root and on every workspace nested in it. A bigger root means a bigger tree.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Example" id="scope_chapter-example">
        <p>You are in <path>top/mid/deep</path>, and each folder is a workspace.</p>
        <code-block lang="shell"><![CDATA[
top/                    topmost
├── api
└── mid/
    ├── infra
    └── deep/           nearest (you are here)
        └── infra-tools
]]></code-block>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <td>Command</td>
                <td>Searches in</td>
                <td>Finds</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>%tool_call% search infra</code></td>
                <td><path>deep</path></td>
                <td><code>infra-tools</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>%tool_call% search infra -s topmost</code></td>
                <td><path>top</path> and everything below</td>
                <td><code>infra</code>, <code>infra-tools</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><code>%tool_call% search infra -s global</code></td>
                <td>The global workspace</td>
                <td>Only what it lists</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="How the root is chosen" id="scope_chapter-resolution">
        <code-block lang="mermaid"><![CDATA[
flowchart TD
    A["--scope"] --> B{value}
    B -->|global| G["global workspace<br/>~/.gws"]
    B -->|nearest and -D| D["the -D folder<br/>no search"]
    B -->|nearest| N["first workspace<br/>going up"]
    B -->|topmost| T["highest workspace<br/>going up"]
    N --> F{found?}
    T --> F
    F -->|yes| R["use it"]
    F -->|no| FB{"global-fallback<br/>and global file?"}
    FB -->|yes| G
    FB -->|no| E["error: no workspace found"]
]]></code-block>
        <list>
            <li>
                With <code>-D &lt;folder&gt;</code> the search starts from that folder. In <code>nearest</code> scope
                the folder is used as it is, even if it is not a workspace.
            </li>
            <li>
                The fallback is on by default. Turn it off with <code>global-fallback: false</code>, see
                <a href="Configuration.topic">Configuration</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
                <code>init</code> refuses <code>--scope global</code>.
            </li>
            <li>
                Another value fails with <code>Invalid workspace mode "x": must be one of nearest, topmost, global</code>.
            </li>
        </list>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="See also" id="scope_chapter-see-also">
